WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.124 --> 00:00:01.709
(audience applauds)

00:00:01.709 --> 00:00:03.198
- Can I sit on your couch?
- Yes.

00:00:03.198 --> 00:00:04.890
(audience applauds)

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:06.449
- [Kelly] You look so great.

00:00:06.449 --> 00:00:07.282
(audience applauds)

00:00:07.282 --> 00:00:08.115
Oh, my gosh.

00:00:08.115 --> 00:00:12.018
- Mama said, mama said,
"Show up with hostess gifts".

00:00:12.018 --> 00:00:12.851
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:12.851 --> 00:00:14.050
I don't know about all y'all,

00:00:14.050 --> 00:00:16.547
but I was raised to show
up with a hostess gift.

00:00:16.547 --> 00:00:17.380
- [Kelly] This is beautiful.

00:00:17.380 --> 00:00:19.640
- So, this is... I have a
few for you, by the way.

00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:21.160
- Oh my gosh, I literally have one.

00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:22.810
So, the only other person to gift me this,

00:00:22.810 --> 00:00:24.440
Gwen Stefani gave me one
for Christmas, one year

00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:25.780
and I still...
- Oh, oh.

00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:26.870
- No, so what I'm saying...
(audience laughs)

00:00:26.870 --> 00:00:29.150
No, what I'm saying is I think
it's such a beautiful gift.

00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:30.530
So, I'm going to hang it on my door.

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:31.530
- [Jamie] Well, of course, so.

00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:32.363
- Yeah.

00:00:32.363 --> 00:00:33.459
- As you know...

00:00:33.459 --> 00:00:34.880
- Because that was in Montana,
I don't have one for here.

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:37.300
- Well, I'm born and raised
in the City of Angels.

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:38.812
I'm a California girl.

00:00:38.812 --> 00:00:41.960
(audience applauds)
- I like it.

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:44.859
- You can clap for a California
girl, anytime you want.

00:00:44.859 --> 00:00:45.781
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:45.781 --> 00:00:48.123
So, we've never met, I was
on your show virtually.

00:00:48.123 --> 00:00:49.730
- [Kelly] Virtually, yes.

00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:53.720
- I started a little, company
called, My Hand in Yours,

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:57.430
which gives comfort items
and celebration items

00:00:57.430 --> 00:00:59.820
to people in times of
crisis and celebration,

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:03.137
with 100% going to Children's
Hospital of Central

00:01:03.137 --> 00:01:05.070
and I mean 100%.
(audience applauds)

00:01:05.070 --> 00:01:06.110
But wait, wait, wait.

00:01:06.110 --> 00:01:08.580
I'm saying it's the only store of its kind

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:11.210
where 100% of what you spend

00:01:11.210 --> 00:01:12.820
is sent to the hospital, literally.

00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:13.653
- [Kelly] That's amazing.

00:01:13.653 --> 00:01:17.160
- This is, with Creekside
Farms, our new, holiday wreath.

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:18.270
- [Kelly] I love it.

00:01:18.270 --> 00:01:21.040
- Which will be offered
on the site and wait...

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:22.590
- [Kelly] Which will
be on my door, tonight.

00:01:22.590 --> 00:01:23.710
- Wait, wait.

00:01:23.710 --> 00:01:25.886
- I love that you bring presents.

00:01:25.886 --> 00:01:29.080
- Well again, Mama said,
"Show up with a hostess gift".

00:01:29.080 --> 00:01:30.830
- Well, you were kind.

00:01:30.830 --> 00:01:33.850
- I invented... I took My Hand in Yours

00:01:33.850 --> 00:01:37.960
and I expanded it to My Paw in Yours,

00:01:37.960 --> 00:01:42.960
because all of us have and
we now have a dog leash,

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:45.085
of My Paw in Yours.

00:01:45.085 --> 00:01:45.918
- Yeah.

00:01:45.918 --> 00:01:49.710
- And then last but not least
and the most important is...

00:01:49.710 --> 00:01:54.710
This is the sculpture, of
a mom's hand with a child.

00:01:54.850 --> 00:01:57.260
You're a mom and a fierce mama,

00:01:57.260 --> 00:01:59.340
you are a fierce mama bear.

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:01.510
And this is the third of the sculptures.

00:02:01.510 --> 00:02:03.230
All of those are available.

00:02:03.230 --> 00:02:05.460
And just one more thing,

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:08.490
we also have a new baby
blanket on the site

00:02:08.490 --> 00:02:09.660
for My Hand in Yours.

00:02:09.660 --> 00:02:11.240
So, all of those are available.

00:02:11.240 --> 00:02:12.073
- That's so cool.

00:02:12.073 --> 00:02:13.870
- On my site, but these are gifts to you,

00:02:13.870 --> 00:02:15.261
because you're awesome.

00:02:15.261 --> 00:02:16.141
(audience applauds)

00:02:16.141 --> 00:02:17.810
- Well, hey, thank you so much.

00:02:17.810 --> 00:02:19.300
And you know, it is really, important

00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:21.610
to point that out, that
100% of the proceeds go,

00:02:21.610 --> 00:02:23.450
because that's not often,
that's not the case.

00:02:23.450 --> 00:02:24.630
- But it's not even the
proceeds, 100% of the sales.

00:02:24.630 --> 00:02:25.900
- Sorry, it's 100% of everything.

00:02:25.900 --> 00:02:26.733
That's amazing.

00:02:26.733 --> 00:02:28.300
- Because that, you know what?

00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:30.410
I've been so blessed in my life,

00:02:30.410 --> 00:02:32.650
my husband and I decided
to underwrite the company,

00:02:32.650 --> 00:02:34.060
which means we pay for everything

00:02:34.060 --> 00:02:36.990
and then anything you buy,
I just send every penny,

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:38.200
directly to the hospital.

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:39.420
And it's... Just so you know,

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:41.520
it's been one of the
greatest thrills of my life,

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:43.460
in a year, one year.

00:02:43.460 --> 00:02:47.530
Last August 4th, we raised $350,000

00:02:47.530 --> 00:02:49.028
for Children's Hospital Central.

00:02:49.028 --> 00:02:49.861
(audience applauds)

00:02:49.861 --> 00:02:50.694
- I love it, the reason
why I brought it up

00:02:50.694 --> 00:02:52.510
is I thought it was an
amazing gift to give someone.

00:02:52.510 --> 00:02:54.690
I've never given, I feel
like I'm a good, gift-giver

00:02:54.690 --> 00:02:56.000
and I've never thought of that.

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:57.250
And speaking of animals,

00:02:57.250 --> 00:02:59.110
I have to ask about a photo you posted.

00:02:59.110 --> 00:03:01.070
So, what's happening here?

00:03:01.070 --> 00:03:01.980
- [Jamie] Oh.
(Jamie laughs)

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:02.970
- [Kelly] What's happening?

00:03:02.970 --> 00:03:04.300
- [Jamie] So...
(Jamie laughs)

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:05.530
- [Kelly] First of all...

00:03:05.530 --> 00:03:07.990
- [Jamie] But the context is crazy.

00:03:07.990 --> 00:03:10.740
So, I had just come back
from Venice Film Festival,

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:13.735
where at the ripe, old age of 62,

00:03:13.735 --> 00:03:15.284
(audience applauds)

00:03:15.284 --> 00:03:19.735
I was presented with a
Lifetime achievement award,

00:03:19.735 --> 00:03:21.480
called the Golden Lion.

00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:23.440
It's a prestigious award,

00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:27.130
from an obviously,
beautiful, film festival.

00:03:27.130 --> 00:03:30.290
And I had just come back, the day before,

00:03:30.290 --> 00:03:33.330
with my Golden Lion and I go to the market

00:03:33.330 --> 00:03:37.200
and there's a golden tiger,
like in line ahead of me.

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:40.080
And I thought, "What's happening here?"

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:41.150
So I took a picture of him,

00:03:41.150 --> 00:03:43.270
this poor guy he's now on television.

00:03:43.270 --> 00:03:44.800
Don't hate me.
(audience laughs)

00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:46.460
I am so, sorry.

00:03:46.460 --> 00:03:48.323
- I love it, I love it, I
think it's really, funny.

00:03:48.323 --> 00:03:50.060
- I didn't know you'd
be on Kelly Clarkson.

00:03:50.060 --> 00:03:52.110
It's not my fault.
- He's face is hidden.

00:03:52.110 --> 00:03:52.943
- She did it.

00:03:54.153 --> 00:03:54.986
- [Kelly] He's face is hidden.

00:03:54.986 --> 00:03:56.150
Hey, when you come out like that,

00:03:56.150 --> 00:03:57.290
you want your picture taken.

00:03:57.290 --> 00:03:58.757
You also have a podcast because
you have like so many jobs.

00:03:58.757 --> 00:04:00.264
- I have so much.

00:04:00.264 --> 00:04:01.097
- You have so many things.

00:04:01.097 --> 00:04:02.020
- I have so much.
(Kelly laughs)

00:04:02.020 --> 00:04:04.080
- So wait, it's called "Good Friend".

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:05.640
So, who's been a friend to get you through

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:07.560
like, really, tough times.

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:10.790
- Well, you know, COVID
was pretty tough and...

00:04:10.790 --> 00:04:11.870
- I thought you were going
to say it was a friend.

00:04:11.870 --> 00:04:12.780
(Kelly laughs)

00:04:12.780 --> 00:04:14.272
- No, no.

00:04:14.272 --> 00:04:16.150
You know, COVID was the reason

00:04:16.150 --> 00:04:18.490
why I invented this podcast
called, "Good Friend"

00:04:18.490 --> 00:04:21.140
because I realized it was
through these friendships

00:04:21.140 --> 00:04:24.750
that I have, like we all did,
that's how we got through it.

00:04:24.750 --> 00:04:27.570
We got through it, communicating, deeply

00:04:27.570 --> 00:04:29.240
with the people that we loved.

00:04:29.240 --> 00:04:33.040
And you know, I couldn't name
anybody on national television

00:04:33.040 --> 00:04:35.290
because then I would be
sliding everybody else.

00:04:35.290 --> 00:04:38.910
But I do find that my
friendships are the thing

00:04:38.910 --> 00:04:42.650
that gets me through
the very, hardest times

00:04:42.650 --> 00:04:44.950
and there are hard times, a lot of tears.

00:04:44.950 --> 00:04:47.380
And then of course, the wonderful times.

00:04:47.380 --> 00:04:49.670
And so, I just decided, you know,

00:04:49.670 --> 00:04:51.960
I'd never hosted anything and I thought...

00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:53.020
- Me neither.

00:04:53.020 --> 00:04:53.960
- Yeah, far out.

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:55.470
And guess what? You're really, good at it.

00:04:55.470 --> 00:04:56.820
- [Kelly] We're doing all
right, we're doing all right.

00:04:56.820 --> 00:04:59.140
- You're doing just fine
there, Kelly Clarkson.

00:04:59.140 --> 00:05:00.610
- I love that though,
that you have those...

00:05:00.610 --> 00:05:03.150
I feel like, speaking of good friends,

00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:05.800
I feel like the older I
get, and it was said to me,

00:05:05.800 --> 00:05:07.280
when I was like, 19
getting in the industry,

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:09.380
it was like, be careful who
you surround yourself with.

00:05:09.380 --> 00:05:10.640
And like... And you're really, only

00:05:10.640 --> 00:05:11.670
are going to have so many friends,

00:05:11.670 --> 00:05:13.970
like at the end of the day,
that are really like, get you.

00:05:13.970 --> 00:05:15.390
And I thought, "How sad",

00:05:15.390 --> 00:05:16.223
this individual telling me this,

00:05:16.223 --> 00:05:18.050
because I had so many friends.

00:05:18.050 --> 00:05:20.090
When in reality, I didn't
have that many friends.

00:05:20.090 --> 00:05:21.570
I had like acquaintances,

00:05:21.570 --> 00:05:23.140
but those good friends
that are there for you,

00:05:23.140 --> 00:05:25.300
in the bad and good, that's amazing.

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:27.220
- Well, and Maria
Shriver referred to them,

00:05:27.220 --> 00:05:28.460
which I had never heard before,

00:05:28.460 --> 00:05:32.694
she referred to them on the
show as "flat tire friends".

00:05:32.694 --> 00:05:33.527
- [Kelly] Oh.

00:05:33.527 --> 00:05:35.810
- She said, "Who are
your flat tire friends?"

00:05:35.810 --> 00:05:37.210
Who are those people you can call

00:05:37.210 --> 00:05:40.830
when you're on the 405,
heading south, at rush hour

00:05:40.830 --> 00:05:42.620
and you get a flat tire?

00:05:42.620 --> 00:05:43.453
- Exactly.

00:05:43.453 --> 00:05:46.362
- And AAA says, it'll be five hours.

00:05:46.362 --> 00:05:50.270
Who do you call? And that level of trust,

00:05:50.270 --> 00:05:52.610
show up, someone who will suit up

00:05:52.610 --> 00:05:54.140
and show up for you, which is crucial.

00:05:54.140 --> 00:05:56.230
- And then also, call you out, yeah.

00:05:56.230 --> 00:05:58.311
- Well, I won't ever call
you out, Kelly Clarkson.

00:05:58.311 --> 00:05:59.144
- What?

00:05:59.144 --> 00:05:59.977
- We're new friends, we're just getting

00:05:59.977 --> 00:06:01.200
to know each other.
- You have to call people out.

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:03.100
That's how you get in,
you have to call them out.

00:06:03.100 --> 00:06:04.753
I don't like people who don't call me out.

00:06:04.753 --> 00:06:05.586
- Okay, by the way, there's the book

00:06:05.586 --> 00:06:06.419
that you could write today.

00:06:06.419 --> 00:06:07.930
- I'm just saying there's
enough turds running around

00:06:07.930 --> 00:06:09.800
that people don't call out.
(Kelly and audience laugh)

00:06:09.800 --> 00:06:12.110
We need to start calling
each other out more.

00:06:12.110 --> 00:06:15.210
- I agree with you.
(audience applauds)

00:06:15.210 --> 00:06:17.850
- I think that's real friendship.

